propose.body:
WHY NOW. `summonSeed` is the index within `con.seeds` of the part of the summon that was refused, and as of lp-fcf387 BOTH verbs carry it — preview and place, hull/seed/self/batch alike. `placement.mjs`'s docstring has promised since it shipped that the field exists 'so a caller can light up the offending part of the shape', and no caller ever has. The panel currently renders one sentence and draws the whole constellation the same colour whether it landed or was refused.

THE WORK, and it is small because the plan renderer already exists: `summon-view.js`'s `planShapes(pocket, bounds, cands, cursor, originCount)` returns plain descriptors that `index.html` turns into SVG. Add the refused summon's seeds as descriptors carrying a `blamed: true` flag for the indices named by the refusals (`summonSeed`, plus `otherSummonSeed` on a self/batch refusal), so the page can draw the offending seed differently from its siblings. The page must stay decision-free — it reads a flag, it does not compute legality — which is what `index-summon-wiring.selftest.mjs` already asserts and must keep asserting.

WHY class-a: `plant/test/summon-view.selftest.mjs` exists and passes, and it already drives a REAL session on the MACRO fixture and reaches hull, pocket, player and self blames. The new assertions go in that file.

WHAT THE GATE MUST CHECK, and the weak version is not enough:
  · for a refused preview AND a refused place of the same geometry, the descriptor set marks exactly the indices the verdict's refusals name — recomputed in the test from `res.refusals`, not read back from the descriptor;
  · a CONTROL that the marked set is a PROPER SUBSET of the summon's seeds. Marking everything passes any 'the blamed seed is marked' check and is exactly the lazy implementation to guard against;
  · a self/batch refusal marks BOTH ends (`summonSeed` and `otherSummonSeed`);
  · a `closure`/`nav` refusal marks NOTHING, because it carries no index — the exemption lp-fcf387 pinned, now enforced at the render layer where a lie would be visible;
  · a SUCCESS marks nothing.

WHY A WEAKER CHECK WOULD NOT DO: asserting 'some seed is marked' passes for an implementation that marks the centre unconditionally, which is the single most likely wrong answer here (the centre is index 0 and it is what a naive loop reaches first). The subset control plus the recomputed-from-refusals comparison are what make it bite.

BOUNDED PATHS: plant/summon-view.js, plant/test/summon-view.selftest.mjs, plant/index.html, plant/test/index-summon-wiring.selftest.mjs.

[CARRIED BY TURN 2: this is vision item 1 work — it changes what a visitor sees — and it was proposed at P1 by turn 1 and never reached the ledger because the outbox was not applied. Re-proposed unchanged.]
